# Section Guidance

For each of the 8 sections, this file gives:
- The **scope description** — what the section is really about, so you focus the pre-LOI prose on the right topics.
- The **post-LOI sub-questions** — the numbered items to answer individually only when the user is in post-LOI mode.

In pre-LOI mode, use the scope description to shape 3–8 sentences of prose per section. Do not answer the sub-questions.
In post-LOI mode, answer every sub-question in order, using NA when the sources don't cover it.

---

## 1. Application & Use Case

**Scope.** This section aims to build a clear, shared understanding of what the product does and the problem it solves. It is intentionally high-level and product-focused.

**Post-LOI sub-questions.**
- 1.1 A full description of the application and the use case.
- 1.2 List of key problems that the product solves.
- 1.3 Access to a live product demo showcasing the main functionalities.
- 1.4 A written product roadmap covering the next 12–24 months, including planned features and their expected timeline.
- 1.5 A written AI-specific roadmap: which AI features are planned, at what stage they are, and the reasoning behind them.
- 1.6 A high-level overview of the pricing model: tiers, structure, and what differentiates each tier.
- 1.7 A description of how users behave in front of the application and the typical user interaction.
- 1.8 A description of the expected lifetime of the solution, including the anticipated trajectory of the architecture over both the short and long term.

